  "worked_solution": "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}\u2061x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x=1-2{sin}^{2}\u2061x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x-1)=-{sin}^{2}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x-\\frac{1}{2}x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\pi )-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
